#NEXUS

[ turner2012a_fig79: Paravian tree, read by eye at 2x. The gold is the drawn tree, with Rahonavis in Unenlagiinae; the two curved arrows mark the alternative placements with the step cost of each (+7, +11) and are not part of the tree. The arrow on the root stem leads to the rest of the tree and is not a tip. Avialae and Troodontidae are open triangles, each one tip named by the word beside it. Paraves, Deinonychosauria, Dromaeosauridae and Unenlagiinae, printed at node brackets or a node circle, are kept as internal labels. Polytomies: the five microraptorines (Tianyuraptor to Hesperonychus), Dromaeosaurus-Achillobator-Atrociraptor-Utahraptor, and Deinonychus-Velociraptor-Balaur-Adasaurus. 24 tips, 3 polytomies (5, 4, 4 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 7 case (census 2, seed 20261241). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

